### User Managment ###

1. To add a User
:/# useradd <username>

2. To add password for the user
:/# passwd <username>

3. To check the user details 
:/# vim /etc/passwd/                                <This will show the user file can use cat>

4. To check the user password
:/# vim /etc/shadow/                                <This will show the encrypted password for user>

5. To delete the user
:/# userdel <username>

# NOTE: If the user forgots the password no one can recover it the password encryption is on way can't be decrypt

6. To add a user with all info
:/# adduser <username>                              <This will prompt to user information with pwd>

7. To change password with specific time 
:/# chage -M 90 username                             <This will reminds user to change password after 90 days>

8. To lock the user 
:/# passwd -l <username>                             <This will lock any hacky or suspicious user>

9. To unlck user
:/# passwd -u <username>

## Working with Groups ##

10. To add a group  
:/# groupadd <groupname>

11. To add a user to the group
:/# usermod -aG <groupname> <username>

12. Viewing Group Memberships
:/# <group> <username>

13. Changing Primary Group
:/# usermod -g new_primary_group <username>